flake	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T20:05:22.7153430Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
flake	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T20:05:22.7164329Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
flake	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T20:05:22.7264151Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
flake	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T20:05:22.7274720Z ^[[0m
flake	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T20:05:22.7275435Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
flake	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T20:05:22.7276441Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
flake	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T20:05:22.7276889Z 
flake	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T20:05:22.7277304Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
flake	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T20:05:22.7278285Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
flake	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T20:05:22.7278797Z 
flake	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T20:05:22.7279143Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
flake	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T20:05:22.7279977Z    if you are ready to continue.
flake	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T20:05:22.7280325Z 
flake	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T20:05:22.7281273Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
flake	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T20:05:22.7281954Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
flake	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T20:05:22.7282516Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
flake	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T20:05:22.7282940Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
flake	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T20:05:22.7283143Z 
flake	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T20:05:22.7283398Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
flake	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T20:05:22.7283708Z 
flake	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T20:05:22.7283942Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
flake	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T20:05:22.7284369Z    can use Nix.
flake	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T20:05:22.7284546Z 
flake	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T20:05:22.7284683Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
flake	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T20:05:22.7284871Z 
flake	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T20:05:22.7287617Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
flake	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T20:05:22.7288416Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
flake	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T20:05:22.7289015Z 
flake	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T20:05:22.7289266Z I will:
flake	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T20:05:22.7289661Z 
flake	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T20:05:22.7290050Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
flake	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T20:05:22.7290672Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
flake	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T20:05:22.7291178Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
flake	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T20:05:22.7291610Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
flake	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T20:05:22.7291930Z  - install Nix in /nix
flake	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T20:05:22.7292234Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
flake	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T20:05:22.7292677Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
flake	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T20:05:22.7293093Z    /root
flake	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T20:05:22.7308558Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
flake	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T20:05:22.7309578Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
flake	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T20:05:22.7320951Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
flake	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T20:05:22.7321708Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
flake	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T20:05:22.7322260Z 
flake	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T20:05:22.7323380Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
flake	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T20:05:22.7324092Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
flake	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T20:05:22.7341769Z 
flake	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T20:05:22.7342403Z ^[[34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
flake	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T20:05:22.7353092Z ^[[0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
flake	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T20:05:22.7353944Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
flake	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T20:05:22.7354737Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
flake	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T20:05:22.7355140Z 
flake	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T20:05:22.7355447Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
flake	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T20:05:22.7355912Z 
flake	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T20:05:22.7357011Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
flake	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T20:05:22.7358135Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
flake	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T20:05:22.7358438Z 
flake	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T20:05:22.7358570Z If you would like to
flake	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T20:05:22.7358896Z see the output, try like this:
flake	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T20:05:22.7359108Z 
flake	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T20:05:22.7359350Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
flake	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T20:05:22.7359776Z   $ sh ./install-nix
flake	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T20:05:22.7359944Z 
flake	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T20:05:22.7359975Z 
flake	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T20:05:22.7360252Z ^[[32m~~> Checking for artifacts of previous installs
flake	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T20:05:22.7365971Z ^[[0mBefore I try to install, I'll check for signs Nix already is or has
flake	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-23T20:05:22.7367059Z been installed on this system.
